About Us
ADW Johnson is a multi-disciplinary company specialising in Urban Design, Planning, Engineering, Project Management, Surveying and Landscape Architecture with offices in Newcastle, the Central Coast, and in Sydney. We are passionate about development and treat each and every project as if it is our own. We use our expertise, dedication and hard work to forge long-term relationships with our clients and deliver best development outcomes. 
About The Opportunity
We are now looking for a Trainee Draftsperson to join our company at our Central Coast office.
With the wide variety of land development, high end residential and infrastructure projects ADW Johnson is involved with, there will be an opportunity to work on diverse projects in a supportive and stimulating environment.
Successful candidates will undertake engineering studies at TAFE, typically one day a week, as part of a recognised traineeship. The remaining four days will be spent in the office where you will be provided on-the-job training and mentoring. In addition to a competitive salary, all TAFE fees for your studies will be reimbursed.
Reporting directly to the Drafting Coordinator some of your responsibilities will include:
·       Plan drafting and communicating with the supervisor in relation to job status; 
·       Liaising with your supervisor and other staff in relation to workload planning and drafting instructions;
·       Working effectively and collaboratively as part of a project team; and
·       Completing quality assurance checklists.
This role offers the following benefits:
·       An exciting opportunity to work with some of NSW's leading developers;
·       Variety of projects, including land development, high-end residential, and infrastructure, from planning through to construction completion;
·       Paid TAFE certification;
·       A tailored career development program for career advancement;
·       A steady stream of interesting projects;
·       A positive work environment with flexible hours and social activities;
·       Competitive salary based on skills and experience;
·       Access to a generous overtime system.
About You 
The ideal candidate will have recently completed their School Certificate or HSC, or begun a Drafting course at TAFE, with a keen interest in pursuing a drafting career. Desired skills include:
·       Excellent communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in a team;
·       Enthusiasm and a passion for the construction and engineering industries;
·       Strong written and verbal communication abilities;
·       A strong work ethic and keen attention to detail.

Devlyn Construction is privately owned and has been established in Western Australia for over 30 years. We are a leading commercial contractor that specialises in delivering projects across a range of sectors in WA’s metropolitan and regional locations.  
We currently have a position for an Estimator to join our Canning Vale operations.
THE ROLE
As an Estimator with Devlyn you will be required to prepare detailed and accurate estimates for a wide variety of projects often with tight deadlines. 
You will work in close liaison with senior management, project managers, architects, clients and subcontractors.
Responsibilities include:
- Document control for tender packages;
- Accurately read and interpret plans;
- Issue quote requests to relevant trades and suppliers;
- Take-offs and estimates using CostX;
- Developing a thorough understanding of tender/project requirements;
- Preparing estimate pricing;
- Assess subcontractor quotes for completeness against project scope;
- Liaise with other internal stakeholders;
- Liaison with subcontractors during and after the tender period;
- Handover to construction team on successful tenders.
ABOUT YOU 
To be successful with Devlyn, the ideal candidate will have:
- Commercial construction and building knowledge;
- Demonstrated ability in working to strict time frames;
- Experience in the analysis and interpretation of tender plans and documents;
- Excellent computer literacy;
- Have excellent attention to detail;
- Have good time management skills with the ability to prioritise workload;
- Strong interpersonal skills; and
- Excellent organisational and communication skills.
ABOUT US
At Devlyn we strive to deliver projects with a difference.
We transform commercial spaces while providing our clients with excellent service and an enjoyable project delivery journey. 
We recognise the importance of being a flexible employer and promote a great team culture - achieving all project objectives with the ability to have a laugh along the way.
By joining the Devlyn team we offer: 
- An attractive and competitive remuneration package;
- Job stability with a strong pipeline of works;
- The ability to work autonomously while maintaining a great support network;
- Market leading internal systems supported by technology.
This is a full-time position with the potential for a long-term career.
HOW TO APPLY 
If you'd like to join a forward thinking team and believe you meet the above criteria please submit your CV via Seek.
We look forward to hearing from you!
You must have a legal right to work in Australia to apply for this position.
